properties.description:
Cut 2026-10-17 on Anthony's word ("Merge 765 and cut 0.86.0"). A minor carrying #763 to #765, the primes trial's fixes:
- #763: a proof counts what it should (a computed check holds a premise only through its kept record; a claim that loses its support reads unsupported, never false; a what-if stays inside the reasoning it affects; a refutation reads as refuted, not as a defect);
- #764: a proof says what it assumes and asks (assumed and discharges; generalizes_over with variables and fixes; independent_of and independent_except; the statement_kind enum; ask_question; the design-a-proof skill);
- #765: corollary and proposition as statement kinds.

200 tools (199 in 0.85.0); the new one is ask_question. The stamp moves by vocabulary, not by type: statement_kind on Requirement and Constraint, plus optional properties; no node or edge type is added. Measured at the cut with the published 0.85.0 binary: it opens a store 0.86.0 wrote and warns, misreads a proof that assumes something (unproven where 0.86.0 reads shown), and refuses 0.86.0's export; 0.86.0 opens 0.85.0's stores and exports unchanged (docs/upgrading-to-v0.86.0.md). Nothing is deprecated or removed; the Anchor type, which 0.85.0 deprecated, is not removed in 0.86.0 and stays deprecated. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
